sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-petroff-kahng-audit-kahng-coral-geometry-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Kahng, Odle & Wakeman (2024) Reef-Coral Colony Geometry & Surface-Area Productivity — Model fidelity to source: 74/100" ;
        rdfs:comment "All seven algebraic functions (`hemisphere_extension`, `hemisphere_sap`, `disc_extension`, `disc_sap`, `cone_extension`, `cone_sap`, `cylinder_sap`, L68-110) are exact consequences of the paper's discrete annual volume rule `V(t+1) = V(t) + G*S(t)/rho` under the stated surface/volume formulas (`V = 2/3 pi r^3, S = 2 pi r^2`; `V = h pi r^2, S = pi r^2`; `V = pi h^3/(3 alpha^2), S = pi h^2 sqrt(1+alpha^2)/alpha^2`; `V = pi r^2 L, S = 2 pi r L`). Deduct 14 points because the script does not contrast the finite 1-yr step (`r(t+1) - r(t)`, which rises from `0.52` to `1.20 cm/yr` in Panel c) against the instantaneous continuum limit `dr/dt = G/rho = 1.25 cm/yr` (where hemisphere linear extension is strictly size-independent); and deduct 12 points because general oblate/prolate hemispheroids and multi-branch colony self-shading are simplified to a spherical hemisphere and single cylinder without explicit boundary notes. Evidence: 2024-kahng-coral-geometry.py L57–L60: empirical parameter dictionaries MASSIVE, BRANCH, DISC, and COMMON <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5564750/2024-kahng-coral-geometry.py#L57-L60>; 2024-kahng-coral-geometry.py L68–L110: exact discrete 1-year extension and SAP formulas for hemisphere, disc, cone, and cylinder <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5564750/2024-kahng-coral-geometry.py#L68-L110>; 2024-kahng-coral-geometry.py L172–L185: panel (c) plots discrete 1-yr extension approaching continuum plateau G/rho and sqrt(2)*G/rho <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5564750/2024-kahng-coral-geometry.py#L172-L185>." ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-kahng-coral-geometry-model-fidelity> ;
        pk:hasProbability "0.74"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-kahng-coral-geometry-model-fidelity> rdfs:label "Kahng, Odle & Wakeman (2024) Reef-Coral Colony Geometry & Surface-Area Productivity (2024-kahng-coral-geometry.py, docs/media/kahng_coral_geometry_growth.gif) satisfies the MorphoEval 0.1.0 criterion 'Model fidelity to source' for Scleractinian reef corals (massive Porites, branching Acropora, plating Leptoseris)" ;
        dcterms:identifier "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Gemini 4 Argon (primary) + Claude Fable 5.1 (independent blinded second assessor)" .
}

